  The countable rational-position/basis-word lemma in the prose is a
  separately proved sufficient condition for <verbatim|Cluster.horizon>. It
  must not be presented as an inspected source implementation of
  <verbatim|Vendor.horizon>. Its assumptions include finite-dimensional raw
  label spaces, multilinearity, and continuity on all of Conf in every phase.
  The character RP paragraph is likewise an explicit operator proof using the
  inspected <verbatim|slim> identity; the paragraph is not a claim that all
  of <verbatim|Vendor.emits> has thereby been constructed.

  <section|Checked external results><label|checked-external-results>

  Shared <verbatim|blueprint/background/README.md> and the available notes
  were searched; there was no accepted matching Gelfand/Riesz note. No shared
  background file is owned or modified by this task.

  <\itemize-dot>
    <item>D. P. Williams, <em|A (Very) Short Course on C>-Algebras*, 14
    February 2024, Theorem 2.13, printed pp. 29\U31, and Theorems 2.17/2.19,
    pp. 33\U34. Author-hosted PDF: <hlink|https://math.dartmouth.edu/~dana/bookspapers/cstar.pdf|https://math.dartmouth.edu/~dana/bookspapers/cstar.pdf>.
    Actual statements inspected through the web reader. The application is to
    the nonzero unital norm-closed commutative star algebra in B(H0); its
    unit acts on a unit vacuum. The Gelfand transform is onto C(X), and
    characters are continuous star homomorphisms. Spectral permanence and
    functional calculus justify positivity in the closed subalgebra. The
    proof of metrizability and full support in the manuscript is specific and
    explicit.

    <item>E. T. Sawyer, <em|Lecture Notes in Advanced Real Analysis>, Chapter
    6, Theorem 32, printed p. 78, author-hosted PDF:
    <hlink|https://math.mcmaster.ca/~sawyer/Publications/Advanced_Real_Analysis.pdf|https://math.mcmaster.ca/~sawyer/Publications/Advanced_Real_Analysis.pdf>.
    Actual positive-functional statement inspected. The compact metrizable
    character space is locally compact Hausdorff and Cc(X)=C(X); the
    transported vacuum functional is positive by the continuous square root
    and has value one on the constant function one. Only its Borel
    representing measure is used. The source's completed sigma algebra is not
    needed here.
  </itemize-dot>

  These are source matches checked by the author, not accepted shared
  references. Independent review of the matches remains necessary. Failed
  fetches of other Riesz notes were not used as evidence.

  <section|Exact outstanding inputs><label|exact-outstanding-inputs>

  <\enumerate>
    <item>The repeated-word bound <verbatim|QRead> must hold with the
    all-arity uniform rate needed for <verbatim|Spread.AllCopy>, not just a
    constant for each fixed arity. <verbatim|YM.OS.irons> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/OS/Halves.lean> reduces this to <verbatim|Tiled>; its
    construction is not yet written. The parent inspected this reduction.

    <item>Full O(4) covariance of the unselected hierarchy is needed for
    <verbatim|Ground.inert> and the cluster exchange argument. Signed
    coordinate symmetries alone do not justify either step.

    <item>Norm separability is now proved from the dense rational slab/label
    family in <verbatim|slab-regularity.tex>; its upstream all-copy and
    raw-slot derivative identities remain inputs. This discharges the earlier
    abstract separability premise.

    <item><verbatim|phase-regularity.tex> proves all-character
    smoothness/caps, phase semigroups, smeared RP and phase all-copy
    transfer. <verbatim|reflection-transport.tex> proves the replication
    variance, ordinary reflection and full O(4) transport, conditional on
    actual bounded real approximations. Stress/differential identity
    production and the upstream hierarchy remain outstanding. These chapters
    now supply the phase semigroup and countable-horizon hypotheses used in
    a.e. selection.

    <item><verbatim|phase-fields.tex> proves the corrected finite-dimensional
    detector argument and common-null retention from explicit
    moment/spanning/injective-limit data. Production of
    <verbatim|Retain.Funds> and those detector properties remains open.

    <item>Relativistic complex heat, joint boundary values, heat-vector
    bridge and field domain are now proved in the subsequent chapters;
    Lorentz covariance, locality, boundary label detection and momentum PVM
    remain. See reconstruction-evidence.md.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Additional inspected correspondence><label|additional-inspected-correspondence>

  <\itemize-dot>
    <item><verbatim|slab-regularity.tex>:
    <verbatim|YM.Work.B02.norm_remainder> (B02/Analysis.lean),
    <verbatim|YM.Work.B02.smooth_place> (B02/Slab.lean): full dense
    matrix-element remainder argument and finite derivative-label bounds, not
    weak-only continuity.

    <item><verbatim|phase-regularity.tex>: <verbatim|YM.Work.B11.phase_cap>,
    <verbatim|YM.Work.B13.answer>, <verbatim|YM.Work.B08.smear>; actual
    all-character powers and joint-test Bochner RP.

    <item><verbatim|reflection-transport.tex>:
    <verbatim|YM.OS.Grid.Covering.square> (Phase/Square.lean),
    <verbatim|YM.Work.B05.answer>, <verbatim|YM.Work.B06.answer>.
    Generic-inside-each-word qualification checked; no all-Conf grid
    approximation assumed without the continuity extension.

    <item><verbatim|phase-fields.tex>: <verbatim|YM.Extraction.Retain.bit>
    (Phase/Detect.lean), <verbatim|YM.Extraction.Retain.lift_detect>
    (Phase/Picks.lean). The parent read the full source proofs and
    <verbatim|Euclid/Null.lean> quotient definitions.
  </itemize-dot>

  All these chapters have independent local agent review. That is evidence,
  not accepted human review; metadata stays null.

  <section|Validation at this stage><label|validation-at-this-stage>

  The parent compiled <verbatim|phases.tex> as part of the standalone draft
  successfully (19 pages before adding phase-selection). <verbatim|python3
  scripts/check_blueprint.py> passed with two units at that checkpoint. No
  new Lean build or axiom audit was run. Subsequent exact compilation, render
  checks, and hashes belong in <verbatim|validation.md> after integration.
  The independent agent's local mathematical review does not change machine
  status from draft.

